SUMMARY:🚀 Falcon 9 Block 5 | Globalstar 2-R Mission 1 (x 8)
LOCATION:Space Launch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Falcon 9 Block 5 | Globalstar 2-R Mission 1 (x 8)\n\nStatus\n
 Launched\n\nLift-off\n01:12 UTC\, Sunday 16 August 2026\n\nProvider\nSpa
 ceX\n\nSite\nSpace Launch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA\n\n
 Orbit\nLow Earth Orbit\n\nMission\nThe Globalstar global mobile communic
 ations network offers global\, digital real time voice\, data and fax se
 rvices via its Low Earth Orbit satellite constellation. The constellatio
 n operates in a 1410 km orbit inclined at 52 degrees. In early 2022\, Gl
 obalstar contracted with MDA for the construction of 17 new 2nd generati
 on refresh satellites to replenish the existing constellation. Rocket La
 b is sub-contracted to build the satellites' buses and the launch dispen
 sers.\n\nLAUNCH DATES SLIP CONSTANTLY - weather\, technical holds and ra
 nge availability move them\, often by days and sometimes by hours on the
  day itself. This calendar rebuilds daily\, but always check before sett
 ing an alarm.
CATEGORIES:SpaceX,Falcon 9
URL:https://nextspaceflight.com/launches/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:TENTATIVE
